                        "form": "stanked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7942f3f6-e8dc-34e8-99c4-1b4598c424bc",
                        "entry_id": "baf5b14d-5d3c-3800-bc39-fe512c5c1c34",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To surround or guard."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb4fdc72-d624-4f40-b5e1-df514670bd74",
                                "sense_id": "7942f3f6-e8dc-34e8-99c4-1b4598c424bc",
                                "text": "This was executed with sch gallantry and spirit by the troops, that, notwithstanding the natural strength of this pos, the abbatis of fruit trees that were made, the batteries of the town of Bommel which stanked the approach, and the considerable number of men who defended it, it was soon carried, and the enemy driven across the river (every where passable on the ice) with considerable loss of men and of four pieces of cannon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfe4fb67-0a8e-4033-8879-7a9203e4768b",
                                "sense_id": "7942f3f6-e8dc-34e8-99c4-1b4598c424bc",
                                "text": "upon the south of the garden, by ane easy descent, you come to the great orch-yaird containing sex aikers of ground, includeing a parcell thereof that is woody, all upon one levine, stanked and hedged, about whose back entry from the south leads you first to a triangle haugh surrounded with wood, and then to the river of Clyde for salmond fishing for more nor two mylles, which makes the lenth of the wholl barronie from Garingill to the Miregill mouth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1432367-2da6-4e32-9f6b-e0e5b7aa1de9",
                                "sense_id": "7942f3f6-e8dc-34e8-99c4-1b4598c424bc",
                                "text": "Upon Friday the 25th of April, sir William Forbes of Craigievar, at his own hand, takes in the place of Kemnay, frae the widow lady thereof, plants some soldiers therein, being stanked about, and of good defence;"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
