                        ],
                        "form": "stanked"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ea8031bb-2b62-46d4-90a4-19aa527e6605",
                        "entry_id": "9f117a67-d1f1-3e0e-b67d-4c19eded66bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "stanked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                        "entry_id": "9f117a67-d1f1-3e0e-b67d-4c19eded66bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To trample."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Cornwall"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a93dd8a-c14c-4180-a292-e1d1facb0cc1",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "In the por ( bustle ) I lost my hat ; tell gittin ' cloase to a mait-stannin ' (shambles), to saave myself from bein' stanked ( trampled ) under fut, I got up and set down 'pon the stannin' ; an ' then, aw, I feelt my sawl all a-fire weth love for everybody theere, and sprengin' to my feet, I begun to ex'ort, and then took to pray."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "939812c0-6f03-4227-a6a4-9337d059164a",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "And then she took down the cloam from the chimbly and stanked it under her feet, so as no one shouldn't hev it after she war gone."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "919b75fc-6f91-4d52-a370-ba130f50399e",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "I like to know a man be stanked on, for they'm miserable torments most o' their time ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1183154d-a42e-4f1f-960f-7b22681b50e3",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "I caan't afford to ' ave my straw stanked down an ' spoiled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55c5d2f7-8c48-406f-921b-b59b33e33787",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "I remarked on this to Tippet and he mumbled something about they saucy girls having gathered all the eating peas and stanked on his lettuces and carrots to get them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce8888e8-0220-422e-9956-9add140b4962",
                                "sense_id": "29c4cf80-8e1e-3b15-ab02-85733b333a24",
                                "text": "It is this moment which Parker chooses to tell; in so doing setting a new agenda and standard for Cornu-English dialect literature: ' We should ha' just stanked on over the top of 'en but instead we hesitated and squared up."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                        "entry_id": "9f117a67-d1f1-3e0e-b67d-4c19eded66bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To stumble or lurch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Cornwall"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "93169979-8903-4d78-88e0-7d9b6914ea6e",
                                "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                                "text": "I put on my clean gook to-day, And went to fetch some barm,When I stanked 'pon a slaw-cripple, Down there by Hodge's farm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ad7e6f0-b089-4264-ad62-c9f696d8170b",
                                "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                                "text": "But she stanked upon a wuilkin one day in the chall, and after that she was always liable to quames."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54346ebf-e1e9-4b7b-ad27-d7b5afa751a4",
                                "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                                "text": "He catched sight o' the barra handles sticked up over a lime bucket, and stanked fore to grab 'em."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40b760a6-8fbc-40f9-83df-0d5820fdbd26",
                                "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                                "text": "Certainly, there would be those happy to support his elevation to parliament: Then up jumped Reuben Gill, And he stanked on the floor To send John Prisk to Parliament He'd beg from door to door."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c48b7a0-eb3e-48b5-9e0c-43dce564b8be",
                                "sense_id": "348e0688-52f8-340b-a84c-dd7a47901668",
                                "text": "The wemmen and some of the men sot down, too, but all the young cheldern runned away down out o' sight, so I stanked out as fast as I cud to see where they was going to, and when I got there, they was all down by a will."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
